Arabic|MR|Mauritania|MRU|NULL|Yes|No|Mauritania has a single national SMIG (salaire minimum interprofessionnel garanti) fixed by decree under the Labour Code. The last figure I can attribute to a specific instrument is 30,000 MRO/month (decree of 2011), which became 3,000 MRU/month after the 2018 redenomination (1 MRU = 10 MRO). I recall press/Council-of-Ministers reports of a raise to about 4,000 MRU/month in the 2023 period, but I cannot name the decree number or its effective date with confidence, so no rate is entered. For the operator's check: at the Labour Code's 40-hour week, 3,000 ÷ 173.33 h = 17.308 MRU/h; 4,000 ÷ 173.33 h = 23.077 MRU/h. Whichever figure is current must be confirmed against the Journal Officiel before use. French is the working language of the administration; Arabic is the official language.|new|Loi n° 2004-017 du 6 juillet 2004 portant Code du Travail (SMIG fixed by decree after opinion of the Conseil National du Travail); implementing decree of 2011 setting the SMIG at 30,000 MRO (now 3,000 MRU); a later decree (c. 2023) reportedly raised it to ~4,000 MRU — number and date not confirmed|Journal Officiel de la République Islamique de Mauritanie / Ministère de la Fonction Publique et du Travail (travail.gov.mr) — exact URL not verifiable from this environment; unsure of the current page|2011 decree (3,000 MRU); reported 2023 raise unconfirmed|monthly|not converted — rate withheld; candidates: monthly 3,000 ÷ 173.33 h = 17.308 · monthly 4,000 ÷ 173.33 h = 23.077 (40 h/week per Labour Code)|low|A only||no — source not reachable from this environment|Enlil
Arabic|EH|Western Sahara|MAD|NULL|No|Yes|Deliberate deferral, not an oversight: Western Sahara publishes no minimum-wage instrument of its own. In the Moroccan-administered territory (Laâyoune-Sakia El Hamra and Dakhla-Oued Ed-Dahab regions, covering the vast majority of the population) Morocco applies its own Labour Code and SMIG/SMAG decrees, so the operative hourly floor is the MA row (MAD). In the areas east of the berm administered by the SADR/Polisario there is no published statutory minimum wage. Because two administrations and two different regimes coexist, no single rate can be stated for the territory; the MA row is the reference for any figure. Arabic is the primary language in both zones (Spanish/French as secondary working languages).|new|None specific to the territory. Moroccan-administered areas: Dahir n° 1-03-194 (Code du Travail, Law 65-99) and the Moroccan SMIG decrees as applied to the southern provinces — see the MA row. SADR-administered areas: no statutory minimum wage identified.|No territory-specific official source. Moroccan-administered areas: Ministère de l'Inclusion économique, de la Petite Entreprise, de l'Emploi et des Compétences (travail.gov.ma) / Bulletin Officiel — same as MA row; not verifiable from this environment|2026 (follows the MA row's effective date)|none|— (see MA row: Moroccan SMIG is published hourly)|medium|A only||no — source not reachable from this environment|Enlil
