Sinhala|LK|Sri Lanka|LKR|105.000|Yes|No|A=B. National Minimum Wage of Workers Act No. 3 of 2016 sets a single national floor for all workers in any industry/service (originally Rs 10,000/month, Rs 400/day), amended by Act No. 16 of 2021 (Rs 12,500 / Rs 500), by Act No. 25 of 2024 (Rs 17,500/month, Rs 700/day, absorbing the budgetary relief allowance; A recalls effective 1 January 2024), and — implementing Budget 2025 — by a 2025 Amendment Act to Rs 21,000/month and Rs 840/day (both agents recall passage in 2025; exact Act number and commencement to verify). If the 2025 amendment is not yet in force the operative figures are Rs 17,500 / Rs 700 (= 87.50/h). The statute publishes both monthly and daily; the daily rate is for an 8-hour working day (Wages Boards Ordinance / Shop and Office Employees Act, 8 h/day, 45–48 h/week), so hourly = 840 ÷ 8; monthly 21,000 = 25 d × 840. Sectoral Wages Boards set higher trade-specific minima above the floor; Budget Relief Allowance Acts historically added fixed allowances. Monthly ÷ 173.33 would give 121.16 — not used, statute defines the day.|new|National Minimum Wage of Workers Act No. 3 of 2016, as amended by Act No. 16 of 2021, Act No. 25 of 2024 and the 2025 Amendment Act|https://www.labourdept.gov.lk (Department of Labour), https://documents.gov.lk (Gazette) and https://www.parliament.lk/acts — cannot be fetched from here|2025 (Rs 21,000/840); 2024 step Rs 17,500/700 held with higher confidence|daily|daily 840 ÷ 8 h = 105.000 (monthly 21,000 ÷ 25 d = 840; monthly ÷ 173.33 would give 121.16)|medium|A=B||no — source not reachable from this environment|Pangu
