English|CX|Australia — Christmas Island|AUD|24.950|Yes|No|Christmas Island is a non-self-governing Australian external territory. There is no territory-specific minimum wage: the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) is applied to the Territory by s 8A of the Christmas Island Act 1958 (Cth), so the Australian National Minimum Wage (NMW) set annually by the Fair Work Commission's Expert Panel is the statutory floor there, in Australian dollars. The figure cited is the NMW fixed by the National Minimum Wage Order 2025 (Annual Wage Review 2024-25): AUD 24.95 per hour / AUD 948.00 per 38-hour week, effective from the first full pay period on or after 1 July 2025. CAUTION: the Annual Wage Review 2025-26 decision (effective 1 July 2026) will have superseded this by today's date (2026-09-12); I cannot confirm its figure from this environment, and the operator's AU row shows 26.440, which may reflect that later order — treat my figure as the last order I can vouch for, not as a correction of his. Award minimum rates above the NMW apply to award-covered employees (as everywhere in Australia); the NMW remains the single national floor, so no_single_rate = false, matching the operator's AU row. Single-sourced (A only); unverifiable from here.|new|Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth), applied to the Territory of Christmas Island by Christmas Island Act 1958 (Cth) s 8A; rate set by the Fair Work Commission's National Minimum Wage Order 2025 (Annual Wage Review 2024-25 decision, [2025] FWCFB 3500 as I recall — PR number not vouched for)|https://www.fwc.gov.au/agreements-awards/minimum-wages-and-conditions/national-minimum-wage (Fair Work Commission; also https://www.fairwork.gov.au/pay-and-wages/minimum-wages) — cannot be fetched from this environment; URL cited from memory|1 July 2025 (National Minimum Wage Order 2025); likely superseded 1 July 2026 by the 2025-26 order, unconfirmed here|hourly|—|medium|A only||no — source not reachable from this environment|Thoth
